{"name":"Euphoria","hex":"#eebbff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"euphoria","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An excited state of joy; a feeling of intense happiness.","Ellipsis of gender euphoria."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/euphoria"}],"entries":[{"title":"Euphoria","blocks":[{"text":"Euphoria is the experience of pleasure or excitement and intense feelings of well-being and happiness. Certain natural rewards and social activities, such as aerobic exercise, laughter, listening to or making music and dancing, can induce a state of euphoria. Euphoria is also a symptom of certain neurological or neuropsychiatric disorders, such as mania. Romantic love and components of the human sexual response cycle are also associated with the induction of euphoria. Certain drugs, many of which are addictive, can cause euphoria, which at least partially motivates their recreational use."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euphoria"},{"title":"Euphoria (American TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Euphoria is an American psychological drama television series created and written by Sam Levinson for HBO. Based on the Israeli miniseries of the same name created by Ron Leshem, the series stars Zendaya as drug-addicted teenager Rue Bennett, who also serves as an unreliable narrator. The ensemble cast includes Maude Apatow, Angus Cloud, Eric Dane, Alexa Demie, Jacob Elordi, Barbie Ferreira, Nika King, Storm Reid, Hunter Schafer, Algee Smith, Sydney Sweeney, Colman Domingo, Javon \"Wanna\" Walton, and Austin Abrams. Dominic Fike, Adewale Akinnuoye-Agbaje, Martha Kelly, Chloe Cherry, and Toby Wallace join later in the series."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euphoria_(American_TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Blue_Crystal_Meth.jpg/500px-Blue_Crystal_Meth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Blue_Crystal_Meth.jpg/1280px-Blue_Crystal_Meth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Blue_Crystal_Meth.jpg/500px-Blue_Crystal_Meth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A large dose of methamphetamine causes a drug-induced euphoria.[38]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Crystal_Meth.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Sam_Levinson_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/500px-Sam_Levinson_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Sam_Levinson_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/1280px-Sam_Levinson_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Sam_Levinson_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/500px-Sam_Levinson_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Series creator, showrunner, and writer Sam Levinson also directs almost all episodes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASam_Levinson_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Zendaya_MTV_Awards_2.jpg/500px-Zendaya_MTV_Awards_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Zendaya_MTV_Awards_2.jpg/500px-Zendaya_MTV_Awards_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZendaya_MTV_Awards_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Hunter_Schafer-64616_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Hunter_Schafer-64616_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimed